                    <death when="1800-10-25"/>
                    <occupation>Illustrator, Artist, Author, Printseller</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Thomas Macklin was an Irish printseller, curator and author who moved to
                            Fleet Street in 1782. His successes included a series called 'Macklin's
                            English Poets' (better known as 'The Poet's Gallery'), and a hugely
                            successful illustrated filio Bible with contributions from artists such
                            as Hugh Douglas Hamilton and Richard Cosway amoung others. </p>
                        <p>It should be noted that Macklin knew and collaborated with Henry Fuseli
                            who painted both Godwin and many of his aquantances mentioned in the
                            diary, and so it is possible that that is how the two met.</p>
                    </note>
